(4681582, 674618, 50695, '<td valign="top">Arthur, upon feeling a great thirst, approached the Lake of Sighs and kneeled before it, but before he could dip his hand into the cooling waters, he saw a shape rise from the deep. ''Twas a Lady of much woe. <br/> <br/>Arthur, moved with sympathy for the Lady, who wept not, but whose sardonic smile was certain sign of inner turmoil, asked "What doth distress thee, Fair Lady?"<br/> <br/>"Ah, I am sore distressed upon my bodice, which doth make my breasts look funny, and therefore twist my face into this wry position."<br/> <br/>"Who hath done this to thee, Fair Lady, to trap thee in this lake and dress thee so funnily?"<br/> <br/>"Ah!" sighed the Lady. "Thus is my woe, for I am trapped by Larus the Great, whose magic surpasseth all human courage."</td>', 'Arthur, upon feeling a great thirst, approached the Lake of Sighs and kneeled before it, but before he could dip his hand into the cooling waters, he saw a shape rise from the deep. ''Twas a Lady of much woe.  Arthur, moved with sympathy for the Lady, who wept not, but whose sardonic smile was certain sign of inner turmoil, asked "What doth distress thee, Fair Lady?" "Ah, I am sore distressed upon my bodice, which doth make my breasts look funny, and therefore twist my face into this wry position." "Who hath done this to thee, Fair Lady, to trap thee in this lake and dress thee so funnily?" "Ah!" sighed the Lady. "Thus is my woe, for I am trapped by Larus the Great, whose magic surpasseth all human courage."', '2008-05-05 11:31:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(4681585, 675827, 29474, '<td valign="top">Seems to be flat and lacking contrast.</td>', 'Seems to be flat and lacking contrast.', '2008-05-05 11:32:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(4681588, 676118, 50695, '<td valign="top">Once upon a time, there lived a Gazebo on the edge of a lake. The Gazebo was very lonely, for no one sat upon it, and all it could do was stare across the lake at a mansion full of happy people who were always cavorting. The Gazebo wanted so badly to be part of that happiness, but could do nothing about it, because, well, it''s just a gazebo. Gazebos don''t do anything.</td>', 'Once upon a time, there lived a Gazebo on the edge of a lake. The Gazebo was very lonely, for no one sat upon it, and all it could do was stare across the lake at a mansion full of happy people who were always cavorting. The Gazebo wanted so badly to be part of that happiness, but could do nothing about it, because, well, it''s just a gazebo. Gazebos don''t do anything.', '2008-05-05 11:33:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(4681604, 675960, 50695, '<td valign="top">Mister Man knew this was his last chance. Without missing a step, he said, "Hey, nice um... stretch pants."<br/> <br/>"Thank you," she said, accompanied by the clopping of her shoes.<br/> <br/>"Yeah, well, um... do you drink coffee?"<br/> <br/>"Only on bad days," she said.<br/> <br/>"Do you want to have a bad day together?" he asked.<br/> <br/>"Better than a bad day alone," she replied. The cobblestones smiled.</td>', 'Mister Man knew this was his last chance. Without missing a step, he said, "Hey, nice um... stretch pants." "Thank you," she said, accompanied by the clopping of her shoes. "Yeah, well, um... do you drink coffee?" "Only on bad days," she said. "Do you want to have a bad day together?" he asked. "Better than a bad day alone," she replied. The cobblestones smiled.', '2008-05-05 11:36:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(4681617, 676202, 29474, '<td valign="top">Although I don''t understand or like this picture, it does intrigue me. Which is what I am expecting from this challenge ... and not finding so far.</td>', 'Although I don''t understand or like this picture, it does intrigue me. Which is what I am expecting from this challenge ... and not finding so far.', '2008-05-05 11:39:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(4681618, 675848, 50695, '<td valign="top">Nana took one last look at her scrapbook and closed it up again, as her grandchildren came into the room. They begged her to look at it, but she refused, as always. She told them that they would only be disappointed, that this was just her childhood, more ordinary than theirs.<br/> <br/>What they didn''t know was that there was not a single photograph in this "chapbook," just pages and pages of formulae and diagrams. Nobody would ever think to look for it here...</td>', 'Nana took one last look at her scrapbook and closed it up again, as her grandchildren came into the room. They begged her to look at it, but she refused, as always. She told them that they would only be disappointed, that this was just her childhood, more ordinary than theirs. What they didn''t know was that there was not a single photograph in this "chapbook," just pages and pages of formulae and diagrams. Nobody would ever think to look for it here...', '2008-05-05 11:40:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(4681626, 675799, 50695, '<td valign="top">Birds have no stories. <br/>They inscribe their passions <br/>in the air, where no mark is left. <br/> <br/>Birds look below to our stories,<br/>patient readers on tree branches,<br/>observing myriad plots,<br/>connected and unconnected,<br/>waiting, perhaps,<br/>for a crumb to fall.</td>', 'Birds have no stories. They inscribe their passions in the air, where no mark is left.  Birds look below to our stories,patient readers on tree branches,observing myriad plots,connected and unconnected,waiting, perhaps,for a crumb to fall.', '2008-05-05 11:43:55.000000', NULL, 1),
