(4697582, 675973, 50551, '<td valign="top">Back on DPC after a long time away and thumbing through recent competitions and I saw this and immediately thought: "ah! must be Gary as Nasti would never leave the hands  in shadow!"<br/> <br/>I lie - this was bound to be Gary. Excellent, mate, and shame about the narrow-minded 1''s.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-05-12 15:36:09.</i></td>', 'Back on DPC after a long time away and thumbing through recent competitions and I saw this and immediately thought: "ah! must be Gary as Nasti would never leave the hands  in shadow!" I lie - this was bound to be Gary. Excellent, mate, and shame about the narrow-minded 1''s.', '2008-05-12 16:35:49.000000', '2008-05-12 16:36:09.000000', 0),
(4697590, 676064, 66384, '<td valign="top">Ha, ha, I tried that once when I was little. I didn''t hide in a suitcase, but on the floor of the back seat of the car. My parents were leaving on a train for a vacation, and I thought if we got to the station, in downtown Detroit, it would be too late for them to take me back home. Didn''t work. They found me before we had gone two blocks. Needless to say, this image resonated with me. I''m so glad enough others felt the same way. Congratulations on your ribbon.</td>', 'Ha, ha, I tried that once when I was little. I didn''t hide in a suitcase, but on the floor of the back seat of the car. My parents were leaving on a train for a vacation, and I thought if we got to the station, in downtown Detroit, it would be too late for them to take me back home. Didn''t work. They found me before we had gone two blocks. Needless to say, this image resonated with me. I''m so glad enough others felt the same way. Congratulations on your ribbon.', '2008-05-12 16:37:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4697615, 674352, 67579, '<td valign="top">Wow, its one thing to read the "story" but to see it captured so well in a single image. Don''t know how this didn''t ribbon, hats off to you :) very well done..<br/> <br/>-dave</td>', 'Wow, its one thing to read the "story" but to see it captured so well in a single image. Don''t know how this didn''t ribbon, hats off to you :) very well done.. -dave', '2008-05-12 16:53:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4697626, 676081, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pineapple:</b></div><hr/><i> The idea is good, IMO.  I wonder what might make for more drama?  Raking light coming in from an out of frame window?  A spilled glass?  Some deep shadow on the arm hinting at the body out of frame?  Just thinking what I might do to enhance the visual theatre. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I agree -- more/better props might have helped. Most of the light is actually coming from a window way off to the left -- see the lighting on the glass and the shadow below the arm; I probably should have made it darker overall, though, but the typical state of people''s monitors made me err on the side of visibility.<br/> <br/>It didn''t want to spill any liquid -- those are some old cards which used to belong to my grandfather and I didn''t want to take a chance with them.<br/> <br/>I only found out just last night that I only have three of the five cards exactly right -- the Eight of Diamonds should be the spade, and the Queen should instead be the Deuce of Spades ... :-(</td>', 'Originally posted by pineapple: The idea is good, IMO.  I wonder what might make for more drama?  Raking light coming in from an out of frame window?  A spilled glass?  Some deep shadow on the arm hinting at the body out of frame?  Just thinking what I might do to enhance the visual theatre.  I agree -- more/better props might have helped. Most of the light is actually coming from a window way off to the left -- see the lighting on the glass and the shadow below the arm; I probably should have made it darker overall, though, but the typical state of people''s monitors made me err on the side of visibility. It didn''t want to spill any liquid -- those are some old cards which used to belong to my grandfather and I didn''t want to take a chance with them. I only found out just last night that I only have three of the five cards exactly right -- the Eight of Diamonds should be the spade, and the Queen should instead be the Deuce of Spades ... :-(', '2008-05-12 17:03:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4697661, 675261, 27373, '<td valign="top">I don''t think people are sick of good ole "TF".  Overall this is probably the best of the images, thus far.  I think however what seperates this from the others is the previous images had more of an immediate "funny bone" impact.  This one almost has a touch of sadness.  I would love to see the tooth fairy getting stuck in a hold up.  Maybe three or four kids, a nice big bag of quarters.... just an off the cuff idea.</td>', 'I don''t think people are sick of good ole "TF".  Overall this is probably the best of the images, thus far.  I think however what seperates this from the others is the previous images had more of an immediate "funny bone" impact.  This one almost has a touch of sadness.  I would love to see the tooth fairy getting stuck in a hold up.  Maybe three or four kids, a nice big bag of quarters.... just an off the cuff idea.', '2008-05-12 17:21:28.000000', NULL, 0),
