(4699576, 676027, 66384, '<td valign="top">I like this double portrait. It really does look like they could be related. I like everything about it except the straps hanging around Dan''s neck. They really annoy me, and I don''t usually get annoyed by photos. I think it''s because everything else is so good. Anyway, to me, the straps break up the composition and take away from the portrait nature of the image. If you were taking a portrait of a photographer the straps would be okay, but I would want to see the camera too. I see that you got a decent score on this, so I guess this wasn''t a big deal for the other voters.</td>', 'I like this double portrait. It really does look like they could be related. I like everything about it except the straps hanging around Dan''s neck. They really annoy me, and I don''t usually get annoyed by photos. I think it''s because everything else is so good. Anyway, to me, the straps break up the composition and take away from the portrait nature of the image. If you were taking a portrait of a photographer the straps would be okay, but I would want to see the camera too. I see that you got a decent score on this, so I guess this wasn''t a big deal for the other voters.', '2008-05-13 15:48:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4699591, 676090, 66384, '<td valign="top">I think you''re right about the box. The tiger would have looked much more abandoned. Here he looks like he has been put down temporarily, perhaps for the night. I like the crop, the lighting, the b&amp;w, and all the vertical lines. I feel a bit frustrated by not seeing his whole face.</td>', 'I think you''re right about the box. The tiger would have looked much more abandoned. Here he looks like he has been put down temporarily, perhaps for the night. I like the crop, the lighting, the b&w, and all the vertical lines. I feel a bit frustrated by not seeing his whole face.', '2008-05-13 15:53:33.000000', NULL, 0),
